 /*                                                                          */
/* This is designed to be run on any computer with a network link to a Pardus */
/* server. This program uses Gtk 4. A user must first successfuly log in      */
/* to a Pardus server using their user name and password. Once logged in,     */
/* that server will only follow instructions from that user till their        */
/* session comes to an end (by error or by log out). However, a logged-in     */
/* user will be given a one-time client_id (unique to that session). If that  */
/* id is transferred to another client program (running on a differnt PC over */
/* a different network but connected to the same Pardus server) then that     */
/* user may continue to control the Pardus server from that different PC      */
/* without having to log in again. The server administrator can limit and     */
/* schedule each user's abilities to use the system to ensure fair            */
/* distribution of resources (stop one user hogging or blocking the system)   */
/* if that is desireable.                                                     */
/*                                                                            */
/* P. J. Tadrous 08.08.2019 - 24.11.26                                        */
/******************************************************************************/

////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
//                                                                            //
// Notes on Compilation                                                       //
// ====================                                                       //
//                                                                            //
//                                                                            //
// Dependencies Common to All Systems                                         //
// ----------------------------------                                         //
// You will need gtk4, libpng, libzmq, libfontconfig and libjpeg (or          //
// jpegturbo) installed and  available to the compiler and linker in order to //
// build this program. You also need the PARDUS header files parddefs.h and   //
// and pardcapdefs.h and the resources file resources.c in addition to this   //
// source file.                                                               //
//                                                                            //
// Linux                                                                      //
// -----                                                                      //
// Compile with:                                                              //
//                                                                            //
// gcc -O2 -march=native `pkg-config --cflags gtk4` -Wall -Wno-format-truncation -o pardclient resources.c pardclient.c `pkg-config --libs gtk4` -lm -lzmq -lpng -ljpeg -lfontconfig -lpulse-simple -lpulse -lX11
//                                                                            //
// In the AppImage I use the `-march=x86-64-v2 -mavx` flag instead of the     //
// `-march=native` flag to ensure good compatibility with all x86 CPU from    //
// about 2011 onwards, Like this:
// gcc -O2 -march=x86-64-v2 -mavx `pkg-config --cflags gtk4` -Wall -Wno-format-truncation -o pardclient resources.c pardclient.c `pkg-config --libs gtk4` -lm -lzmq -lpng -ljpeg -lfontconfig -lpulse-simple -lpulse -lX11
// If you are compiling for your own PC then use the `-march=native` flag as  //
// shown in the first command so you get the best for your own CPU.           //
//                                                                            //
// Windows MSYS2 UCRT64                                                       //
// --------------------                                                       //
// gcc -O2 -march=native `pkg-config --cflags gtk4` -Wall -Wno-format-truncation -o pardclient.exe resources.c pardclient.c `pkg-config --libs gtk4` -lws2_32 -lm -lzmq -lpng -ljpeg -lfontconfig -lwinmm

// For compiling on macOS, see the full user manual.                       //
//                                                                            //
////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////


